{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Debugging and Profiling Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 1: Print Debugging (Yes, It Works)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Print debugging gets dismissed. It shouldn't. For tensor code, a targeted print statement beats stepping through a debugger because you need to see shapes, dtypes, and value ranges all at once."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def debug_print(name, tensor):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{name}: shape={tensor.shape}, dtype={tensor.dtype}, \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"device={tensor.device}, \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"min={tensor.min().item():.4f}, max={tensor.max().item():.4f}, \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"mean={tensor.mean().item():.4f}, \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"has_nan={tensor.isnan().any().item()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Call this after every suspicious operation. When the bug is found, remove the prints. Simple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 2: Python Debugger (pdb and breakpoint)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The built-in debugger is underrated for AI work. Drop `breakpoint()` into your training loop and inspect tensors interactively."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def training_step(model, batch, criterion, optimizer):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inputs, labels = batch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outputs = model(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = criterion(outputs, labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if loss.item() > 100 or torch.isnan(loss):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        breakpoint()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "When the debugger drops you in, useful commands:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `p outputs.shape` to check shapes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `p loss.item()` to see the loss value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `p torch.isnan(outputs).sum()` to count NaNs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `p model.fc1.weight.grad` to check gradients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `c` to continue, `q` to quit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is conditional debugging. You only stop when something looks wrong. For a 10,000-step training run, that matters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 3: Python Logging"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Replace print statements with logging when your debugging goes beyond a quick check."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import logging"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logging.basicConfig("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    level=logging.INFO,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    format=\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    handlers=["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logging.FileHandler(\"training.log\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logging.StreamHandler()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logger.info(\"Starting training: lr=%.4f, batch_size=%d\", lr, batch_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logger.warning(\"Loss spike detected: %.4f at step %d\", loss.item(), step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logger.error(\"NaN loss at step %d, stopping\", step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Logging gives you timestamps, severity levels, and file output. When a training run fails at 3 AM, you want a log file, not terminal output that scrolled off screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 4: Timing Code Sections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Knowing where time goes is the first step to optimization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Timer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, name=\"\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.name = name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __enter__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.start = time.perf_counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __exit__(self, *args):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elapsed = time.perf_counter() - self.start"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"[{self.name}] {elapsed:.4f}s\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with Timer(\"data loading\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch = next(dataloader_iter)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with Timer(\"forward pass\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outputs = model(batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with Timer(\"backward pass\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Common finding: data loading takes 60% of training time. The fix is `num_workers > 0` in your DataLoader, not a faster GPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 5: cProfile and line_profiler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "When you need more than manual timers:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python -m cProfile -s cumtime train.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This shows every function call sorted by cumulative time. For line-by-line profiling:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install line_profiler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@profile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(model, data, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    output = model(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = F.cross_entropy(output, target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Run with: kernprof -l -v train.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 6: Memory Profiling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### CPU Memory with tracemalloc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import tracemalloc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tracemalloc.start()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# your code here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = build_model()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data = load_dataset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "snapshot = tracemalloc.take_snapshot()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "top_stats = snapshot.statistics(\"lineno\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for stat in top_stats[:10]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(stat)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### CPU Memory with memory_profiler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install memory_profiler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from memory_profiler import profile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@profile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def load_data():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    raw = read_csv(\"data.csv\")       # watch memory jump here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    processed = preprocess(raw)       # and here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return processed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run with `python -m memory_profiler your_script.py` to see line-by-line memory usage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### GPU Memory with PyTorch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "if torch.cuda.is_available():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(torch.cuda.memory_summary())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Allocated: {torch.cuda.memory_allocated() / 1e9:.2f} GB\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Cached: {torch.cuda.memory_reserved() / 1e9:.2f} GB\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "When you hit OOM (Out of Memory):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Reduce batch size (first thing to try, always)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Use `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` to free cached memory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Use `del tensor` followed by `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` for large intermediates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4. Use mixed precision (`torch.cuda.amp`) to halve memory usage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "5. Use gradient checkpointing for very deep models"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 7: Common AI Bugs and How to Catch Them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### Shape Mismatch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The most frequent bug. A tensor has shape `[batch, features]` when the model expects `[batch, channels, height, width]`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def check_shapes(model, sample_input):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Input: {sample_input.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hooks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def make_hook(name):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def hook(module, inp, out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            in_shape = inp[0].shape if isinstance(inp, tuple) else inp.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out_shape = out.shape if hasattr(out, \"shape\") else type(out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"  {name}: {in_shape} -> {out_shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return hook"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for name, module in model.named_modules():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        hooks.append(module.register_forward_hook(make_hook(name)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model(sample_input)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for h in hooks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h.remove()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run this once with a sample batch. It maps every shape transformation in your model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### NaN Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "NaN loss means something exploded. Common causes:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Learning rate too high"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Division by zero in custom loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Log of zero or negative number"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Exploding gradients in RNNs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def detect_nan(model, loss, step):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if torch.isnan(loss):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"NaN loss at step {step}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for name, param in model.named_parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if param.grad is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if torch.isnan(param.grad).any():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    print(f\"  NaN gradient in {name}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if torch.isinf(param.grad).any():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    print(f\"  Inf gradient in {name}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### Data Leakage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Your model gets 99% accuracy on the test set. Sounds great. It's a bug."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def check_data_leakage(train_set, test_set, id_column=\"id\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    train_ids = set(train_set[id_column].tolist())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_ids = set(test_set[id_column].tolist())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    overlap = train_ids & test_ids"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if overlap:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"DATA LEAKAGE: {len(overlap)} samples in both train and test\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Also check for temporal leakage: using future data to predict the past. Sort by timestamp before splitting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### Wrong Device"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Tensors on different devices (CPU vs GPU) cause runtime errors. But sometimes a tensor silently stays on CPU while everything else is on GPU, and training just runs slowly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def check_devices(model, *tensors):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model_device = next(model.parameters()).device"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Model device: {model_device}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, t in enumerate(tensors):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if t.device != model_device:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"  WARNING: tensor {i} on {t.device}, model on {model_device}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 8: TensorBoard Basics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "TensorBoard shows you what's happening inside training over time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install tensorboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.utils.tensorboard import SummaryWriter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "writer = SummaryWriter(\"runs/experiment_1\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(num_steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = train_step(model, batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    writer.add_scalar(\"loss/train\", loss.item(), step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    writer.add_scalar(\"lr\", optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"], step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step % 100 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for name, param in model.named_parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            writer.add_histogram(f\"weights/{name}\", param, step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if param.grad is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                writer.add_histogram(f\"grads/{name}\", param.grad, step)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "writer.close()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Launch it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tensorboard --logdir=runs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What to look for:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Loss not decreasing**: Learning rate too low, or model architecture issue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Loss oscillating wildly**: Learning rate too high"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Loss goes to NaN**: Numerical instability (see NaN section above)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Train loss decreasing, val loss increasing**: Overfitting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Weight histograms collapsing to zero**: Vanishing gradients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Gradient histograms exploding**: Need gradient clipping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Part 9: VS Code Debugger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For interactive debugging, configure VS Code with a `launch.json`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"version\": \"0.2.0\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"configurations\": ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"name\": \"Debug Training\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"type\": \"debugpy\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"request\": \"launch\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"program\": \"${file}\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"justMyCode\": false"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Set breakpoints by clicking the gutter. Use the Variables pane to inspect tensor properties. The Debug Console lets you run arbitrary Python expressions mid-execution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Useful for stepping through data preprocessing pipelines where you want to see each transformation."
      ]
    },
